WEBVTT

00:01:59.436 --> 00:02:04.876
I immediately recognized them
as large vertebrae

00:02:04.876 --> 00:02:07.716
from the spine of an ichthyosaur,

00:02:07.756 --> 00:02:10.476
or as it’s colloquially known
as a sea dragon.

00:02:11.156 --> 00:02:14.036
Now, I do need to clear
that name up just a little bit,

00:02:14.036 --> 00:02:17.876
because, I'm sorry to say,
they're not dragons.

00:02:17.916 --> 00:02:19.156
Sorry.

00:02:19.196 --> 00:02:21.116
They're also not swimming dinosaurs.

00:02:21.716 --> 00:02:24.196
They’re not the Loch Ness
Monster on tour either.

00:02:24.836 --> 00:02:27.756
And they're most definitely not,
as the BBC dubbed them

00:02:27.756 --> 00:02:30.076
"Sea dragon dinosaur dolphin fossils."